kunzite: Adreno 710, glue plan K5-min (main repo ios/gpu-glue-plan.md 3.1, 4): surfaces for the
GPU path. SweetSurface's three raw `gpu` boot-arg reads become the hardware layer's answers:
redwood_gpu_on() (the GPU path runs this boot: topaz gpu=1, kunzite keep mode) and
redwood_gpu_identity() (GPU addresses are physical). Scanout slots (S1) are off whenever the GPU
path runs; the 64 guard rows (S5a) come with redwood_gpu_on(), since RedwoodGPU's translated
import takes no surface without them; the GPU pool (S2), the 12 MB reserves (S5b, and
sweet_res_give, S6) and contiguous memory (S5c) only when both answer true, so never on kunzite,
where the SMMU translates and 0x90000000 is the modem's. The presenter's copy (F6): a surface
the GPU drew (drawn != 0, not pool memory) whose last submission is done gets its rows cleaned and
invalidated (sweet_dcache_flush, dc civac) before the memcpy, so no line the CPU held from before
is copied as old pixels. Left for later: RedwoodGPU's wrapDelta, read-only client memory and
gpu_cached=0 (glue plan 3.2). Test: comes with U4 (kgpu=21 kgpu_keep=1, backboardd on the GPU);
without GPU boot-args nothing changes.

